 4274 013370             ! ============================================================
 4275 013370             ! PLOTP RUNTIME -- implementation inherited from v0.10a
 4276 013370             !
 4277 013370             !       PLOTP x,y,f
 4278 013370             !
 4279 013370             ! f=1:
 4280 013370             !       Hybrid operation.
 4281 013370             !       1. ROM360 MOVE x,y ; DRAW x,y ; MOVE x,y
 4282 013370             !          -> CRT/plotter graphics path, ending pen-up at the point.
 4283 013370             !       2. Independently map x,y through the active ROM360 SCALE and
 4284 013370             !          explicitly SET the corresponding CRT pixel if it lies on-screen.
 4285 013370             !          This guarantees the raster result even if a zero-length DRAW is
 4286 013370             !          not rendered as a CRT pixel by the ROM360 vector path.
 4287 013370             !
 4288 013370             ! f=0:
 4289 013370             !       CRT-only CLEAR of the mapped pixel.  No plotter output.
 4290 013370             !
 4291 013370             ! f=2:
 4292 013370             !       CRT-only XOR of the mapped pixel.  No plotter output.
 4293 013370             !
 4294 013370             ! Invalid f values are a no-op, matching LINE semantics.
 4295 013370             !
 4296 013370             ! PLOTP deliberately reuses PAINT's PX/PY/PF, PMODE, PXC/PYC, PTARG and
 4297 013370             ! ROWBUF helpers.  Commands are not re-entrant, so no additional large
 4298 013370             ! working area is required.
 4299 013370             ! ============================================================
 4300 013370             
 4301 013370 241                 BYT 241
 4302 013371             
 4303 013371 232         PLOT.   SAD
